# Contributing to {{SITE_NAME}}

Thanks for considering a contribution — bug reports, docs fixes, and code
are all welcome.

## Before you start

- Check open issues and PRs first so you don't duplicate work in flight.
- For anything larger than a small fix (a new feature, a breaking change,
  a significant refactor), open an issue to discuss the approach *before*
  writing the code. It saves everyone a rewrite.
- Read `AGENTS.md` if you're using an AI coding agent to help — it has
  project-specific conventions the agent should follow, and governance
  rules about what an agent should and shouldn't do unilaterally in this
  repo.

## Making a change

1. Fork the repo and create a branch from the default branch.
2. Make your change, following the conventions in `AGENTS.md`.
3. Add or update tests for anything behavioral.
4. Run `bin/verify.sh` and make sure it passes. It checks the project, migrations, tests,
   seed idempotency and (when Playwright is installed) takes screenshots of key pages.
   Look at the screenshots for any change that affects how a page looks.
5. Open a pull request with a clear description of *what* changed and
   *why* — link the related issue if there is one.

## Commit messages

Clear, present-tense, one logical change per commit where practical.
Conventional Commits (`feat:`, `fix:`, `docs:`, ...) are welcome but not
required.

## Review process

This project currently has a single maintainer. Reviews happen as time
allows — please be patient, and feel free to ping the issue/PR after a
week or two of silence.

## Reporting bugs and requesting features

Please use the issue templates — they ask for the information that's
usually needed to act on a report, and filling them in gets you a faster
response.

## Code of Conduct

This project follows the `CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md` in this repo. By
participating, you're agreeing to abide by it.

